IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja2-part5-ca-capital`

-- Tests for ss 60G to 60M. Expected values are written from the text of the sections, not from the code.

-- s 60G(1): "Subject to section 60I, before making a PACC application, the applicant must apply to the Court of Appeal for, and obtain, the permission"
#ASSERT (`s 60G(1) the applicant has obtained the permission of the Court of Appeal before making the PACC application, as the section requires` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- permission obtained: the requirement is met
#ASSERT (`s 60G(1) the applicant has obtained the permission of the Court of Appeal before making the PACC application, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- section 60I applies: the subsection yields to it
#ASSERT (`s 60G(1) the applicant has obtained the permission of the Court of Appeal before making the PACC application, as the section requires` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(1) the applicant has obtained the permission of the Court of Appeal before making the PACC application, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(2)
#ASSERT (`s 60G(2) the application for PACC permission may be heard and determined by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal despite section 50(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(2) the application for PACC permission may be heard and determined by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal despite section 50(1)` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(3): a period prescribed by the Rules of Court, which are not among the sources
#ASSERT (`s 60G(3) the application for PACC permission is fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 14) 14) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(3) the application for PACC permission is fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 14) 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(3) the application for PACC permission is fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 14) 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(3) the application for PACC permission is fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` NOTHING 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(4)
#ASSERT (`s 60G(4) the applicant files the written submissions and other documents within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 21) 21) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(4) the applicant files the written submissions and other documents within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 21) 22) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(4) the applicant files the written submissions and other documents within the prescribed period, as the section requires` NOTHING 22) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(5)
#ASSERT (`s 60G(5) the respondent files written submissions within the prescribed period` (JUST 14) 14) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(5) the respondent files written submissions within the prescribed period` (JUST 14) 15) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(5) the respondent files written submissions within the prescribed period` NOTHING 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(6)
#ASSERT (`s 60G(6) the person may extend or abridge the period` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(6) the person may extend or abridge the period` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(6) the person may extend or abridge the period` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(7): the four matters the Court of Appeal must consider
#ASSERT (`s 60G(7) the Court of Appeal has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether to grant the application, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(7) the Court of Appeal has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether to grant the application, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(7) the Court of Appeal has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether to grant the application, as the section requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(7) the Court of Appeal has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether to grant the application, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(7) the Court of Appeal has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether to grant the application, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(8)
#ASSERT (`s 60G(8) the application for PACC permission may be summarily dealt with by a written order without being set down for hearing` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(8) the application for PACC permission may be summarily dealt with by a written order without being set down for hearing` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(9): before summarily refusing, must consider the applicant's submissions; may, but need not, consider the respondent's
#ASSERT (`s 60G(9)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily refusing, as the section requires` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(9)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily refusing, as the section requires` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(9)(b) the Court of Appeal is required to consider the respondent's written submissions before summarily refusing` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(9)(b) the Court of Appeal is required to consider the respondent's written submissions before summarily refusing` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(10): before summarily granting, must consider both
#ASSERT (`s 60G(10)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily granting, as the section requires` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(10)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily granting, as the section requires` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(10)(b) the Court of Appeal has considered the respondent's written submissions before summarily granting, as the section requires` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(10)(b) the Court of Appeal has considered the respondent's written submissions before summarily granting, as the section requires` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(11): at the three stages, an incidental direction or interim order as the Court considers necessary, or taking additional evidence
#ASSERT (`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` `s 60G(11)(b) when granting an application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` `s 60G(11)(c) when summarily granting an application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(e) taking additional evidence` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` `s 60G(11) at another stage` `s 60G(11)(e) taking additional evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11) another measure` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(12): "if it thinks additional evidence needs to be taken" and "where" a single Judge, or 3 or any greater uneven number, deals with it: a failed "if" or "where" is the text's no
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge deals with the application` TRUE 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge deals with the application` TRUE 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge deals with the application` FALSE 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 5) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 4) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(12)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` FALSE 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60G(13): "if the Court of Appeal does not grant the application ... no further proceedings may be taken"
#ASSERT (`s 60G(13) the bar on further proceedings in respect of the PACC application applies` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(13) the bar on further proceedings in respect of the PACC application applies` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60G(14): proceedings against the PACP's counsel are not prevented
#ASSERT (`s 60G(14) subsection (13) prevents the proceedings` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(14) subsection (13) prevents the proceedings` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60G(15): not to be granted unless the new material could not have been adduced earlier
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the Court of Appeal may grant the application for PACC permission` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the Court of Appeal may grant the application for PACC permission` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the Court of Appeal may grant the application for PACC permission` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "unless" is met: the bar is lifted, but the subsection does not itself grant permission
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the Court of Appeal may grant the application for PACC permission` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no finding of abuse of process: the "if" is not met, so the prohibition is not triggered and the grant-named function is silent (NOTHING); the bar-phrased twin says the bar does not apply (JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05, part (b))
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the Court of Appeal may grant the application for PACC permission` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the Court of Appeal may grant the application for PACC permission` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the bar-phrased twin: a finding of abuse of process and no new material that could not have been adduced earlier: the bar applies
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the bar on granting the application for PACC permission applies` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the bar on granting the application for PACC permission applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the bar on granting the application for PACC permission applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the unless is met: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the bar on granting the application for PACC permission applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no finding of abuse of process: the bar does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 60G(15) the bar on granting the application for PACC permission applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 60H(1): "Subject to section 60I, where the Court of Appeal grants the application for PACC permission, the PACC application must be made ... and fixed for hearing within such period as is prescribed"
#ASSERT (`s 60H(1) the PACC application is made to the Court of Appeal and fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE (JUST 30) 30) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(1) the PACC application is made to the Court of Appeal and fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE (JUST 30) 31) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(1) the PACC application is made to the Court of Appeal and fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE NOTHING 31) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the "where" is not met: permission was not granted
#ASSERT (`s 60H(1) the PACC application is made to the Court of Appeal and fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` FALSE FALSE (JUST 30) 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- section 60I applies
#ASSERT (`s 60H(1) the PACC application is made to the Court of Appeal and fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE (JUST 30) 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60H(2), (3)
#ASSERT (`s 60H(2) the applicant files the documents in support within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 14) 14) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(2) the applicant files the documents in support within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 14) 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(2) the applicant files the documents in support within the prescribed period, as the section requires` NOTHING 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(3) the respondent files the documents in relation to the application within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 14) 14) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(3) the respondent files the documents in relation to the application within the prescribed period, as the section requires` (JUST 14) 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(3) the respondent files the documents in relation to the application within the prescribed period, as the section requires` NOTHING 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60H(4)
#ASSERT (`s 60H(4) the person may extend or abridge the period` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(4) the person may extend or abridge the period` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(4) the person may extend or abridge the period` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60H(5)
#ASSERT (`s 60H(5) the Court of Appeal may exercise the power and make the order` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(5) the Court of Appeal may exercise the power and make the order` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(5) the Court of Appeal may exercise the power and make the order` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60H(6)
#ASSERT (`s 60H(6) the PACC application may be summarily dealt with by a written order without being set down for hearing` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(6) the PACC application may be summarily dealt with by a written order without being set down for hearing` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60H(7)
#ASSERT (`s 60H(7)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily refusing, as the section requires` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(7)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily refusing, as the section requires` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(7)(b) the Court of Appeal is required to consider the respondent's written submissions before summarily refusing` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(7)(b) the Court of Appeal is required to consider the respondent's written submissions before summarily refusing` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60H(8): "Except where subsection (7) applies", must consider both
#ASSERT (`s 60H(8) the Court of Appeal has considered both sets of written submissions before summarily deciding the PACC application on its merits, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(8) the Court of Appeal has considered both sets of written submissions before summarily deciding the PACC application on its merits, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(8) the Court of Appeal has considered both sets of written submissions before summarily deciding the PACC application on its merits, as the section requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(8) the Court of Appeal has considered both sets of written submissions before summarily deciding the PACC application on its merits, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60H(9)
#ASSERT (`s 60H(9) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage of the PACC application` `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(e) taking additional evidence` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(9) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage of the PACC application` `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(9) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage of the PACC application` `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission` `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60H(9) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage of the PACC application` `s 60G(11) at another stage` `s 60G(11)(e) taking additional evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60H(10)
#ASSERT (`s 60H(10) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges of the Court of Appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60H(10) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges of the Court of Appeal` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 60I(1): while a specified application is pending, no subsequent application unless the Court of Appeal gives permission
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the PACP can make a subsequent application for PACC permission or a subsequent PACC application` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the PACP can make a subsequent application for PACC permission or a subsequent PACC application` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- nothing pending: the "where" is not met, so the prohibition is not triggered and the grant-named function is silent (NOTHING); the bar-phrased twin says the bar does not apply (JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05, part (b))
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the PACP can make a subsequent application for PACC permission or a subsequent PACC application` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the PACP can make a subsequent application for PACC permission or a subsequent PACC application` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the bar-phrased twin: a specified application is pending and the PACP has no permission: the bar applies
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the bar on a subsequent application applies to the PACP` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the unless is met: the bar is lifted
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the bar on a subsequent application applies to the PACP` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- nothing pending: the bar does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the bar on a subsequent application applies to the PACP` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60I(1) the bar on a subsequent application applies to the PACP` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60I(2): the three things the Court of Appeal may do
#ASSERT (`s 60I(2) the Court of Appeal dealing with the specified application may do it` `s 60I(2)(a) grants permission for the PACP to adduce further material when dealing with the specified application`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60I(2) the Court of Appeal dealing with the specified application may do it` `s 60I(2)(b) grants permission for the PACP to make the subsequent application separately under section 60G or 60H`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60I(2) the Court of Appeal dealing with the specified application may do it` `s 60I(2)(c) refuses to grant permission under paragraph (a) or (b)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60I(2) the Court of Appeal dealing with the specified application may do it` `s 60I(2) does something else`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60I(3): "When dealing with any specified application or subsequent application" ("when" counts as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT (`s 60I(3) the Court of Appeal may give the direction` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60I(3) the Court of Appeal may give the direction` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60I(3) the Court of Appeal may give the direction` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 60J(1): "Where any application or action by a PACP ... is filed in a court other than the Court of Appeal"
#ASSERT (`s 60J(1) the Court of Appeal may determine whether the specified application is, or the specified action contains, an application for PACC permission or a PACC application` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(1) the Court of Appeal may determine whether the specified application is, or the specified action contains, an application for PACC permission or a PACC application` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(1) the Court of Appeal may determine whether the specified application is, or the specified action contains, an application for PACC permission or a PACC application` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60J(2)
#ASSERT (`s 60J(2) the determination may be made by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal despite section 50(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(2) the determination may be made by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal despite section 50(1)` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60J(3): "If the Court of Appeal makes a determination ... may do either"
#ASSERT (`s 60J(3) the Court of Appeal may do it` TRUE `s 60J(3)(a) proceeds to determine the specified application, or that part of the specified action, in accordance with section 60G or 60H`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(3) the Court of Appeal may do it` TRUE `s 60J(3)(b) strikes out the specified application or specified action, in whole or in part`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(3) the Court of Appeal may do it` TRUE `s 60J(3) does something else`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60J(3) the Court of Appeal may do it` FALSE `s 60J(3)(a) proceeds to determine the specified application, or that part of the specified action, in accordance with section 60G or 60H`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60J(4)
#ASSERT (`s 60J(4) the Court of Appeal may make incidental directions, give interim orders or take additional evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(4) the Court of Appeal may make incidental directions, give interim orders or take additional evidence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60J(5)
#ASSERT (`s 60J(5)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge makes the determination` TRUE 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(5)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge makes the determination` TRUE 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(5)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge makes the determination` FALSE 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(5)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(5)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 7) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(5)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 2) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60J(5)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` FALSE 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 60K: "Nothing in this Division affects the operation of Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010."
#ASSERT (`s 60K the provision affects the operation of Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60K the provision affects the operation of Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60L: "only by the Court of Appeal"
#ASSERT (`s 60L the court may grant a stay of execution of the death sentence` `Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60L the court may grant a stay of execution of the death sentence` `General Division`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60L the court may grant a stay of execution of the death sentence` `Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60L the court may grant a stay of execution of the death sentence` `District Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60M(1): "When dealing with any application or action" and "on its own motion or upon the application of the Attorney-General or the Public Prosecutor" ("when" and "upon" count as "where")
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1) the Court of Appeal may decide whether to make a finding of abuse of process` TRUE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1) the Court of Appeal may decide whether to make a finding of abuse of process` TRUE FALSE (JUST `Attorney-General`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1) the Court of Appeal may decide whether to make a finding of abuse of process` TRUE FALSE (JUST `Public Prosecutor`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1) the Court of Appeal may decide whether to make a finding of abuse of process` TRUE FALSE (JUST Accused)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1) the Court of Appeal may decide whether to make a finding of abuse of process` TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1) the Court of Appeal may decide whether to make a finding of abuse of process` FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1)(a) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in the case of a relevant application` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1)(a) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in the case of a relevant application` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1)(a) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in the case of a relevant application` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1)(b) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in order to delay or frustrate the carrying out of the sentence of death` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1)(b) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in order to delay or frustrate the carrying out of the sentence of death` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60M(1)(b) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in order to delay or frustrate the carrying out of the sentence of death` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60M(2): the matters, by kind of application; the list is not closed
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(a) an application for PACC permission` `s 60M(2)(a)(i) whether the PACC application to be made is based on material that could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before the relevant date`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(a) an application for PACC permission` `s 60M(2)(a)(ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel obtained the material, and the reasons for the delay`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(a) an application for PACC permission` `s 60M(2)(a)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 60G(4)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(b) a PACC application` `s 60M(2)(b)(i) whether the PACC application was based on material that could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before the relevant date`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(b) a PACC application` `s 60M(2)(b)(ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel obtained the material, and the reasons for the delay`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(b) a PACC application` `s 60M(2)(b)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 60H(2)`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(c) an application for review permission` `s 60M(2)(c)(i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(c) an application for review permission` `s 60M(2)(c)(ii) whether the application for review permission was filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or counsel obtained the material mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(c) an application for review permission` `s 60M(2)(c)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 394H(3) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(d) a review application` `s 60M(2)(d)(i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(d) a review application` `s 60M(2)(d)(ii) whether the application for review permission granted in respect of the review application was filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or counsel obtained the material mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(d) a review application` `s 60M(2)(d)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 394I(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a matter listed for one kind of application is not listed for another
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(b) a PACC application` `s 60M(2)(a)(i) whether the PACC application to be made is based on material that could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before the relevant date`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` `s 60M(2)(a) an application for PACC permission` `s 60M(2)(c)(i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 60M(3): "where a relevant application is heard before a single Judge"
#ASSERT (`s 60M(3) a finding under subsection (1) may be made by that Judge despite section 50(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(3) a finding under subsection (1) may be made by that Judge despite section 50(1)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 60M(4)
#ASSERT (`s 60M(4)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge hears the relevant application` TRUE 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(4)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge hears the relevant application` TRUE 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(4)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge hears the relevant application` FALSE 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(4)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(4)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 9) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(4)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` TRUE 4) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 60M(4)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` FALSE 3) EQUALS JUST FALSE
